+[Part 4] packaging: harden the native archive converter
+
+Validate compressed section headers before using their declared sizes
+as relocation bounds. Accept the known zlib and zstd types and require
+zero or power-of-two alignment.
+
+Require zero-width relocation markers other than R_X86_64_NONE to lie
+inside their target section, and explicitly reject RELR sections in
+archive members.
+
+Log inherited architecture options and signal handler states at startup;
+output failures are ignored. Keep malformed diagnostic environment flags
+nonfatal, and preserve the existing conversion commands, summary fields
+and log lines.
+
+Restore SIGCHLD after helper child cleanup and after every converter
+entry-point exit, including argument parsing. Keep the child signal mask
+unchanged while publishing the process-group ID. Reject a second GNU
+archive long-name table, including an empty first table. Pass the RPM
+debugfiles.list path explicitly and retain the installed identity
+checks.
